IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `yoa-diversion`
IMPORT `yoa-qa`

-- Young Offenders Act 1994 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (yoa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the three roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none:
-- the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value of
-- that input under which the situation does not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise
-- for you`. These two groups are generated by the scratchpad script gen_cases.py from the layer's own parameter lists.
--
-- Then, for the young person (the baseline's seat), each question is asked where its situation holds, with the answer
-- worked by hand and, beside it, the answer equal to the baseline export's on the same facts. For the other roles each
-- question is asked with the answer worked by hand from the deposited text. Jake's facts are the baseline's (born 30
-- August 2006; the shop theft of 20 November 2021; the team of 14 February 2022); the rest is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE quietly takes OTHERWISE for an ASSUMEd value (graffiti finding 31). The
-- layer's helpers over `How my matter ended` list every value; the baseline's reads of `Police option`, `Schedule
-- status`, `What I said`, `Team term`, `Sentence` and `Purpose` go through OTHERWISE, so for those inputs the "not
-- read" cases rest on the parameter script's check that the role and the situation are read first.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked role` IS A Role
ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked option` IS A `Police option`
ASSUME `an unasked schedule` IS A `Schedule status`
ASSUME `an unasked admission` IS A `What I said`
ASSUME `an unasked term` IS A `Team term`
ASSUME `an unasked ending` IS A `How my matter ended`
ASSUME `an unasked sentence` IS A `Sentence`
ASSUME `an unasked purpose` IS A `Purpose`

`as the young person` MEANS `I am, or was, a young person dealt with by police for an offence`
`as the parent` MEANS `I am a parent or other responsible adult of a young person dealt with for an offence`
`as the victim` MEANS `I am the victim of an offence by a young person`
`as the publisher` MEANS `I would publish or pass on information about someone else's matter`

`Jake's birthday` MEANS Date 30 8 2006
`the shop theft` MEANS Date 20 11 2021
`the team day` MEANS Date 14 2 2022

§§ `Each question, for each role it is not about (every other input ASSUMEd)`

